From 0f1dae6a457bfcdf64673ad5c2eb70e51e1c77ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ajim Gulab Mujawar <ajimmujawar007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:23:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: wire the L2 fuzzy layer into the live check pipeline
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fuzzy (L2), semantic (L3) and hybrid-scoring modules were implemented
and unit-tested but never called by run_check — the API ran exact
(L0/L1) detection only. A lightly paraphrased passage (synonym swaps,
reordering) still shares winnowing fingerprints with its source, so L1
retrieves it, but seed-extend needs a 30-char exact run to seed and finds
none — so the source was silently dropped and the check reported 0% on
plainly derived text. The README advertised "Exact + Fuzzy + Semantic"
and "The L2/L3 layers now close this gap"; in the running system neither
did.

This wires L2 into run_check: for each query chunk, the candidates that
seed-extend produced no verbatim passage for are run through the existing
combined token/n-gram/LCS fuzzy scorer; those clearing a threshold are
emitted as match_type="fuzzy" passages. The source is provably already in
the candidate pool, so this adds recall without widening retrieval, needs
no new dependencies (pure Python), and runs off the hot L1 scan path.

Threshold (default 0.4) is set from the measured score distribution: it
sits above the ~0.14 floor where independent same-topic prose scores (no
false positives on honest work) and below the ~0.45 moderate-paraphrase
signal. Heavy paraphrase is deliberately left to L3 — surface overlap
cannot separate it from independent writing.

New knobs on FingerprintConfig: fuzzy_enabled (NOPLAG_FUZZY_ENABLED),
fuzzy_threshold (NOPLAG_FUZZY_THRESHOLD). Setting fuzzy_enabled=False
reproduces the exact-only behaviour. match_type already flows through
persistence and the API/frontend, so fuzzy evidence is distinguishable
from verbatim with no schema change.

Also:
- Fix CI: ruff check (a required CI step) was failing on 24 errors, all
  in the VeriScholar-added modules — unused imports, unsorted imports,
  str+Enum -> StrEnum, raise ... from err, zip(strict=). Ignore RUF002/
  RUF003 project-wide (deliberate typographic punctuation in prose).
- Make the README honest: L2 is now live; L3 is implemented but not yet
  wired into the automatic pipeline (needs a corpus embedding-index build
  step), and heavy paraphrase remains out of scope until then.

Tests: new tests/test_fuzzy_align.py (8) for the fuzzy alignment stage;
new DB-backed workflow tests covering the paraphrase-caught,
fuzzy-disabled-reproduces-exact, and verbatim-not-double-flagged cases.

